// DRAFT (temp) -- prototype only, linked from the "Draft (temp)" nav folder
// in Header.astro. Fifth pass -- first real reimagining rather than a mirror
// of symptom-guide-v2.astro. Same family (tokens, facet vocabulary, the
// cross-page handoff), deliberately different structure:
//
// Symptom Guide is presenting symptoms -- what you notice around the house.
// This page is differential diagnosis -- the reasons those signs show up,
// which is a different kind of question and doesn't resolve the same way.
// A headache doesn't diagnose itself; the same is true of a crack. So
// instead of grouping the 26 causes by soil mechanism (Group A-F, which is
// accurate but not how a homeowner would ever think about their own house),
// they're grouped into three diagnostic tiers built directly from the
// verdict field that was already on every entry:
//   Tier 1  Rule This Out First   (verdict-weak   -- 11 causes)
//   Tier 2  Needs a Closer Look   (verdict-conditional -- 9 causes)
//   Tier 3  Usually Structural    (verdict-strong -- 6 causes)
// Mechanism (Group A-F) still lives on each entry and still shows in the
// opened drawer -- it didn't stop being true, it's just not the lens the
// page opens with anymore.
//
// Also carries the one objective bugfix proven necessary on symptom-guide-v2:
// score() can no longer rank a cause above zero without an actual observed
// "what are you seeing" match -- foundation type/onset/site alone can no
// longer out-rank a real symptom match. And unmatched cards, once you've
// checked something, are now actually hidden behind the "other causes" strip
// instead of just losing their drawer -- the strip's own copy already implied
// they'd be out of view.
//
// Content itself (all 26 entries) is unchanged. Facet vocabulary synced with
// symptom-guide-v2's expanded set (chimney, monolithic slab, spread footing)
// so a handoff either direction pre-checks correctly.
//
// Sixth pass: dropped the per-card A1/C3-style code badge (a relic of the
// old Group A-F layout, unread by any script). Dropped the search bar --
// with the tier structure doing the organizing, it didn't have a place.
// Added a "Try this yourself first" homeowner action item wherever one
// genuinely exists -- most of Tier 1 (plumbing/water bill, drainage,
// irrigation, trees, animal burrows), plus a handful of Tier 2/3 causes
// with a real partial piece even though the overall fix is structural
// (checking gutters on the fill side of a cut-and-fill house, keeping
// moisture steady for expansive clay, keeping water off an adobe wall's
// base, digging up paperwork from a prior repair). Left off the causes
// with nothing genuine to add -- a static pre-existing condition, a
// regional issue nobody controls, something only a professional can
// assess -- rather than inventing a step that isn't real.
